00:21:29.169 --> 00:21:32.059
Please check out NCBI at the Docker hub.

00:21:32.059 --> 00:21:36.899
[Peter] I have a question that is general
and should probably be addressed.

00:21:36.899 --> 00:21:42.820
It has to do with what data are publicly accessible
and I think it's worth talking about the difference

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:47.080
between the controlled access data and the
data that is not controlled access.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:52.649
And what do you have to do to get to those
things.

00:21:52.649 --> 00:21:54.149
[Yuriy] Right.

00:21:54.149 --> 00:21:57.759
We have public data that's available right
now.

00:21:57.759 --> 00:22:03.929
For controlled access, human data, you would
need to get access to that data set through

00:22:03.929 --> 00:22:06.230
dbGaP first.

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:08.770
That data is available in the cloud as well.

00:22:08.770 --> 00:22:15.870
If you have access to datasets through dbGaP
you can access them in the cloud.

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:18.720
[Peter] Thank you.

00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:19.720
Another question.

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:25.490
